@@ -122,9 +122,10 @@ By default a call on the other channel never moves **PTT**. You choose.
 ### The wait after a call
 
 The radio has one receiver, so it switches between A and B. When a call ends, it stays on that channel for 1 s so it
-hears the reply. While it waits, it takes short looks at the other channel. A call there shows **Busy** but doesn't
-interrupt: when the wait ends, the radio goes to it. Change the wait with **Settings > Talk > Dual watch delay**
-(0.5 s to 5 s). Shorter finds the other channel sooner; longer keeps more of a reply that starts late.
+hears the reply. While it waits, it checks the other channel briefly. A signal found there shows **Busy**, including
+on digital channels where the radio detects activity by signal strength. The radio goes there when the wait ends.
+Change the wait with **Settings > Talk > Dual watch delay** (0.5 s to 5 s). A shorter wait finds the other channel
+sooner, and a longer one leaves more time for a reply.
 
 ### Talk back
 
